    "audit_item": "Header Clamp - Check for full compression of lock washer. Bolt should be tightened to manufacturers specification. \nSpine Clamp Hardware - Check for full compression of lock washer. Bolt should be tightened to manufacturers specification.\nTruss Splice Plate - Check for full compression of lock washer. Bolt should be tightened to manufacturers specification.\nSplice Joint - All bolt should be in contact with track. Check track for alignment and that  wheel rolling surface is flash.\nHoist Trolley - Check clevis pin. Check cotter pin. (Cotter pin should be fully wrapped around clevis pin) Check clevis pin bolt and hardware.\nEnd Stops - Check for full compression of lock washer. If thru bolt is exposed, replace end stops.\nVacuum Hoist Clamp - Check for full compression of lock washer.\nWheels - Check for cracks, puts, and grooves: all of these increase pull force. If any of these conditions exists. wheel should be replaced.\nAluminum Bridge Hardware -  Check that lock washers are compressed and nuts tightened to torque specification. Ensure sheer lug hardware is required position and tight.\nEnd Trucks - Check for proper clamping hardware attachment. Ensure correct position on bridge to match specified cantilevers. Inspect end truck wheels following instruction for wheel above. Make sure body of is free of any bent materials, cracked or broken welds. Check overall condition of tubes. Examine support for bent materials, cracked or broken welds. Inspect hardware attaching end truck support tubes. Check wheel plate attachment bolts for any wear and make sure the nylock nut is still in the correct position.",
